  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Trimming and native AOT: every entry point now carries RequiresUnreferencedCode and RequiresDynamicCode, so an application published trimmed or AOT is warned at build time instead of failing in deployment - relevant beyond PublishAot, since trimming is on by default for Blazor WebAssembly and MAUI release builds. Registering a serializer per row type is the documented way out, and that path no longer reflects: the lookup behind CustomSerializers matches by type test rather than by reading a type's interfaces.",
